# Agent harness state: session transcripts, logs, caches and vendored
# native binaries (>150 MB each, over GitHub's 100 MB limit). Local only.
#
# `.omp/*` rather than `.omp/`, and then one negation: git never descends into
# an excluded *directory*, so `!.omp/skills/` under a `.omp/` rule would be
# silently ineffective. Project skills are committed -- they are procedure that
# belongs to the repository, not to whoever happened to run the agent.
.omp/*
!.omp/skills/

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# M-006: Open SciVis volumes are fetched by scripts/fetch_volumes.sh and
# verified against the publisher SHA-512, never committed. The provenance
# beside them is committed; the bytes are not.
docs/measurements/volumes/*.raw
docs/measurements/volumes/*.part

# The published site: eight rendered pages, ~107 MB of copied GIFs and
# screenshots, and three 36 MB wasm modules. Regenerated by
# scripts/build_web.sh and deployed by the `pages` CI job, never committed --
# the wasm alone is well past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit and would double
# the clone for every contributor. The sources under web/ are committed.
web/dist/

# Claude Code's per-machine state, for the reason the `.omp/*` rule above gives.
# Only the `.local` half is machine-specific -- it is this checkout's permission
# grants on this laptop. `.claude/settings.json`, and anything under
# `.claude/skills/` or `.claude/agents/`, is procedure that belongs to the
# repository, so this ignores the one file rather than the directory: git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, and excluding `.claude/` wholesale
# would silently un-commit those the day someone adds one.
.claude/settings.local.json
